# Raw Claude session logs — LOCAL ONLY.
#
# A session log is an uncontrolled capture surface: some of these are full
# Claude Code sessions (one is 2400+ lines with 800+ tool-call blocks) carrying
# arbitrary file contents, absolute paths, and machine state from unrelated
# work. Nothing sensitive turned up in a scan, but "a grep found nothing" is
# not a guarantee worth publishing on.
#
# The provenance lives in session.public.jsonl instead — an allowlisted
# extract (role / model / text and nothing else) produced by the flow-song
# skill's filter-session.sh. That file IS committed; this one never is.
session.jsonl
